00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:54.070
Julien Marchand: Alright, so linear…

47
00:04:54.250 --> 00:05:00.180
Julien Marchand: Is a world that can be used in two contexts for linear mainnet and linear stack.

48
00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:06.160
Julien Marchand: What we are interested in in this case is the Linna stack. So the Linna stack is,

49
00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:12.660
Julien Marchand: It's, software that, has been developed for the past, a bit more than 3 years now.

50
00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:18.910
Julien Marchand: is used to run and operate the LIDA mainnet, which is independent.

51
00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:31.140
Julien Marchand: The Linux stack, is a Layer 2 software, ZK EVM, a pure ZK EVM, that implements, direct by optimization.

52
00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:39.909
Julien Marchand: Which includes, therefore, some, Bazoo plugins, for the execution, for the tracing.

53
00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:46.160
Julien Marchand: Which includes a consensus flyer, the finalization tag, stack, and the bridging.

54
00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:50.410
Julien Marchand: The objective is to offer,

55
00:05:50.550 --> 00:06:05.029
Julien Marchand: High throughput, low cost transaction for enterprises, with, instantaneous finality, at the Layer 2 level, and fast finality at the Layer 1 level with, zero-knowledge proofs.

56
00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:15.909
Julien Marchand: It is, at the moment, developed already in open source. It is under Apache dual licensing, Apache 2, and MIT license.

57
00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:24.689
Julien Marchand: It is, funded and developed by the Linear Consortium and, with… and Consensus.

58
00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:40.669
Julien Marchand: So, it has two main dependent projects, that belong to LFTT. The first one is obviously Bezu. Linna can be, seen as a…

59
00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:50.219
Julien Marchand: an extension of, like, a significant extension of Bezu to transform Bezu into a Layer 2 basic AVM.

60
00:06:50.820 --> 00:07:04.439
Julien Marchand: So obviously we have a lot of, dependency on Bezu, first as a sequencer, with the sequencer plugins for other types of nodes inside, the linear, layer 2.

61
00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:12.920
Julien Marchand: Including for the finalization stack, so generating all the price that's required to prove a transaction.

62
00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:27.289
Julien Marchand: The second main dependent project is Web3j. A part of our codebase is in Java and Kotlin, and as such, we leverage Web3j for most of the,

63
00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:34.940
Julien Marchand: layer interactions, Layer 1 interactions and Layer 2 interactions, from the, from the,

64
00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:37.030
Julien Marchand: from the Java encryption method.

65
00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:47.260
