66
00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:54.620
Julien Marchand: what I would like to emphasize is the commitment to decentralization of the LINA stack.

67
00:07:54.930 --> 00:08:00.860
Julien Marchand: At multiple levels, from a governance point of view.

68
00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:15.139
Julien Marchand: We recently, created the linear consortium outside of, of Consensus, who operates and, and, finance the development of the, of the protocol.

69
00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:24.139
Julien Marchand: We are implementing, multiple features as well for the network to be more and more, decentralized.

70
00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:29.550
Julien Marchand: We already have,

71
00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:44.350
Julien Marchand: I think 88 contributors on the monorepo codebase, and, and a few on, I mean, some more on, the, on the other, Gita project that we have.

72
00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:50.030
Julien Marchand: The focus of the stack is mostly for enterprise and institutions.

73
00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:55.139
Julien Marchand: who offer, production-ready, Layer 2.

74
00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:58.570
Julien Marchand: That can be customized for enterprise adoption.

75
00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:08.079
Julien Marchand: Yeah, that's… this is the main, the main motivation.

76
00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:19.650
Julien Marchand: If we look at the main components that are part of this, donation to LFDT, so it includes the,

77
00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:31.440
Julien Marchand: Layer 2 execution layer… so execution layer as in, like, I mean, yeah, that's, not Bezu, all the plugins that we have that modify Bezu to power the Layer 2.

78
00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:43.190
Julien Marchand: It includes MARU, which is a consensus layer, that can be, that implements the QBFT consensus algorithm.

79
00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:52.940
Julien Marchand: That can be used to drive the execution layer. So this… we decided to implement this consensus layer to…

80
00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:57.420
Julien Marchand: follow what was happening on the Ethereum mainnet.

81
00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:03.940
Julien Marchand: Specifically, so that, basically to follow the trend and be future-proof,

82
00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:15.269
Julien Marchand: And we have decided to pick the QBFT algorithm because this is something that has been used, widely inside Bezoo, and other enterprise software.

83
00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:28.750
